# ONLY credentials stay local. Everything else in this project is tracked so
# the build can continue from a clone on any machine. Learner's call.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local machine config
.claude/settings.local.json

# /data/ is TRACKED now — the kernel-test images are the evidence slices 1-2
# produced, and they travel with the clone. Note this means generated panel
# art gets committed too, so the repo grows with every run.

# The pre-existing UI mockup is now TRACKED, so the look can be ported from a
# clone on any machine. It is pre-existing work and `6-ship` still has to
# disclose it in the README — being in the repo makes that obligation more
# visible, not less. See checklist.md > Revisions.

# Safety net: generated art anywhere. Scoped so the hand-made logo
# files in /assets stay tracked.
/public/chapter/
/public/generated/
*.generated.png
*.generated.webp

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
.next-*/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# Local-store backups written before every save (slice 16, CR-14): a recovery
# copy for the desk, never part of the record.
/data/**/project.json.bak

# The local desk's job records and cross-process lock files (slice 18): working
# state of a running studio, never part of the record.
/data/jobs/
/data/**/*.lock
/data/**/*.lock.d/

# Slice 21's runtime records on the local desk: public shares, visitor reports,
# a person's defaults, trailer records, and what the studio makes (exports,
# videos). Working state of a running studio, like the jobs — never the record.
/data/shares/
/data/reports/
/data/settings/
/data/videos/
/data/outputs/

